Democratic senator Bernie Sanders who  you probably know is also running for  president in 2020 is now calling for the  House of Representatives to immediately  start an impeachment inquiry into Donald  Trump and despite the fact that what he  wants is an impeachment inquiry there  have been a ton of posts and discussions  and comments online which initially said  bernie is calling for Trump's removal  and that's just not what Bernie did  Bernie is calling for the removal of  Trump by voting him out in 2020 that's  one way that Bernie Sanders is saying  Donald Trump should be removed but  Bernie Sanders has only called for the  beginning of an impeachment inquiry  that's step one in the impeachment  process interestingly this happened at a  campaign rally late last week it was not  mentioned for days by media outlets and  when it was initially mentioned a lot of  the reaction to the story was completely  misunderstanding what it is that Bernie  Sanders said so this is the right call  that Bernie Sanders is making and Bernie  Sanders like the David Pakman show  like other shows we all realized that  the Republican Senate is not going to  convict Donald Trump and actually remove  him from office but the facts support  starting an impeachment inquiry period  and that's why I'm glad Bernie's doing  this he said at this rally in Henderson  Nevada quote I believe the House  Judiciary Committee should begin  impeachment inquiries that is inquiries  not impeachment to determine whether or  not  Trump has committed impeachable offenses  this is an important change not because  Bernie saying it will make impeachment  more of a reality more quickly but  because it's starting to become a  distraction does Bernie not think there  should be an impeachment inquiry  what's wrong with Bernie why isn't  Bernie willing to say it well now Bernie  Sanders has made it clear that he  supports an impeachment inquiry but I've  got to make this same statement again  that I've been saying for a while an  impeachment inquiry is not impeachment  and impeachment is not removal okay  the process is inquiry during which  there is testimony investigation debate  by the house if they determine that  impeachment articles should be filed  though  articles are then filed by the house  they require a majority simple majority  50% plus one of the 435 House members  then there is a trial of sorts that the  house puts forward all of the evidence  they believe supports the impeachment of  the president at which point the Senate  votes on whether to convict and remove  the president or not and to convict you  need 2/3 of the Senate all we're talking  about here all that Bernie Sanders is  talking about is an impeachment inquiry  so there are a whole bunch of wrong  reactions to this news the first wrong  reaction to this news is that many have  said Oh  Bernie's calling for the removal of  Trump but that's not what he's doing  it's just not it's wrong in two ways  number one  Bernie's just calling for the inquiry  which happens before impeachment  articles are even filed and number two  even impeachment by the house wouldn't  remove Trump only a conviction by the  Senate would remove Trump and it's not  gonna happen  okay that's not the point the point is  we want to expose what Trump has done  and potentially weaken him in 2020 there  are others who are reacting to this  saying Bernie so weak he's riding the  fence  he's only calling for an inquiry he  should just buckle down and call for  impeachment it's a silly criticism  Bernie's a senator Bernie would  conceivably be one of the people voting  on the trial that would be brought forth  by these articles of impeachment if they  were ever filed it would be in a sense  inappropriate for Bernie to say now we  must remove Trump what most senators  have been saying is that they believe  either an inquiry should start or that  the house should file articles and then  later the Senate would ultimately be  making the decision about how do they  want to vote and do they get that  two-thirds support so Bernie's one  hundred percent correct here he's saying  do the inquiry that's the required first  step it's great news maybe it'll put  more pressure on people like Nancy  Pelosi who have been sort of hesitant to  consider impeachment and Bernie Sanders  is you know some people will criticize  him for this but I believe that the the  net positive benefit of him just saying  this and getting it out of the way makes  sense I'm glad he did it I agree let's  start that inquiry as soon as humanly  possible
 

